course: dictionary
lesson: 10900
title: Visa: official permission
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A visa is an official stamp or document. It is permission from a country to enter it, stay there, study there or work there for a certain time.
explain: Look at the clues in the context: «a visa is official permission to come and stay». Official and permission tell you that the government allows it. A visa is not just something you want or hope for.
explain: Watch the capital letter. Visa with a capital V is the name of a company whose logo is on bank cards. Check the sentence to see which meaning the writer means.
fact: A visa is a noun: one visa, two visas.
fact: «Visa» means official permission to enter, stay in, study or work in a foreign country for a certain time.
fact: Phrases you may hear are apply for a visa, tourist visa, work visa, student visa and visa-free.
fact: Visa with a capital V is the name of a card company; people say «I'll pay by Visa».
fact: An immigrant moves into a new country, and someone who emigrates moves away from their own country.
exercise: «A visa is official permission to come and stay.» What is a visa? | A kind of passport photo | *An official stamp or document that gives permission to enter and stay in a country | A ticket for a train | A bank card with a logo on the front
exercise: Riya says, «I'll pay by Visa.» What is Visa here? | *The name of a card company | An official stamp in her passport | A job she wants to apply for | A country she is going to visit
exercise: Which phrase is for someone who goes to a foreign school? | *Student visa | Work visa | Visa-free | Tourist visa
test: Which word means a person who moves into a new country? | *Immigrant | Visa | Emigrant | Tourist
test: Before the trip you must ___ for a work visa. | forget | *apply | pay | lose
exam: Mia's family want to move abroad to work for a year. Which document do they need to stay there legally? | *A work visa | A tourist visa | A school report | A bank card
